```
id: SPL-001
name: Windows logon failures from one source
description: High number of failed logons (4625) from a single source host or address.
platform: Splunk
mitre_tactic: Credential Access
mitre_technique: T1110 Brute Force
severity: Medium
data_source: index=wineventlog (Security)
false_positives: Expired credentials on services or mapped drives; vulnerability scanners.
tuning: Exclude scanners and known management hosts via a lookup; raise the threshold for
   servers with many service logons.
test_method: Generate 25 failed logons against a lab host with a wrong password.
owner: <OWNER>
status: Draft
last_review: 2026-11-19
```
index=wineventlog sourcetype="WinEventLog:Security" EventCode=4625 earliest=-1h
| where isnotnull(src) AND src!="-" AND src!="::1"
| stats count AS failures dc(user) AS distinct_accounts values(user) AS accounts min(_time) AS first_seen max(_time) AS last_seen BY src, host
| where failures>=20
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)
| sort - failures
